# Pair terms: post hoc

Generated by `posthoc.py` after the registered run; medians (min–max) over the six models; held-out R² on two-cell test decisions.

| model of H on two-cell decisions | R² |
|---|---|
| MLP on the pair alone: s1, s2 (one-hot), w, step | 0.770 (0.503–0.800) |
| MLP on the pair + the tail of the belief (mass and entropy outside the two cells) | 0.796 (0.565–0.857) |
| MLP on the full belief b | 0.880 (0.729–0.926) |
| MLP on b + the pair | 0.857 (0.679–0.909) |
| a table by ordered pair ⊗ [1, w] + step, pairs seen ≥ 30 times (0.78 (0.68–0.88) of decisions) | 0.656 (0.406–0.852) |
| MLP on b on the same decisions | 0.790 (-573.676–0.913) |

**Hedging, posed properly.** Where a shortest-path move from both cells exists and the likelier cell also has shortest-path moves that are not common (2858 (672–5682) decisions): the model takes a common move in 0.11 (0.01–0.45), any likelier-cell move in 0.23 (0.08–0.64); given a likelier-cell move, it is a common one in 0.46 (0.08–0.71) against a chance share of 0.50 (0.50–0.50).

**Landmark seeking.** The share of moves that are shortest-path moves toward the nearest landmark, from the true cell: two-cell decisions 0.26 (0.16–0.50) (chance, a uniformly random move: 0.32 (0.28–0.36)), near-certain decisions 0.16 (0.13–0.22) (chance 0.30 (0.29–0.30)), all decisions 0.24 (0.21–0.29); from the likelier cell: two-cell 0.27 (0.16–0.53), near-certain 0.16 (0.13–0.22).
